doc(names[0],titles[0],f'''The original read-only baseline has {len(baseline['files'])} copied dirty/untracked files with individual SHA256 hashes, the binary working-tree diff, all eight required Git command outputs and the exact commit log. [Baseline](evidence/git-baseline-and-attribution.json), [preservation](evidence/source-preservation-hashes.json). Untracked files were copied as bytes; they are not falsely described as Git-backed.

Actual HEAD/origin/ahead match the historical headline. Gemini's detailed 13-commit list does not match the actual `git log`; several reported hashes/descriptions are invented placeholders. The baseline command output is authoritative. Existing Phase07/08/09/10.1 files and all earlier reports remain in place.

Codex-only diffs compare the pre-audit working copy to current source, not HEAD to current source. Previously clean source uses the unchanged HEAD as its known baseline. Review [the exact path ledger](evidence/changed-files-and-rollback.json) and raw `codex-diffs/` patches before any selective reversal. Never apply a broad Git restore/reset/clean or delete untracked designer files.

One shortened DigitalYes Skip label was observed outside the recorded class-change patch; its current compatible wording was retained and role queries now match the semantic Skip action. Do not attribute unrecorded concurrent wording to Codex. Build source manifests bind the final frozen runtime to captures; earlier exploratory runs where source/spec changed are retained as diagnostic evidence, not final acceptance.''')

doc(names[1],titles[1],'''Gemini claims 35 locally verified gates and one external gate. All 25 JSON files exist and parse; their existence and valid syntax do not substantiate the values. [Validation inventory](evidence/gemini-evidence-validation.json) saves hashes and top-level keys.

The registry really has ten dedicated families and 38 aliases. The advertised “three dedicated suites” is not supported by three newly created files: the package names two new suites, while `registry/phase10Contract.test.jsx` is a pre-existing differently numbered contract suite. Unit/template counts are reconciled by the fresh command logs, not copied from 721.

The 11 claimed layout files are present; the actual package also changes `playwright.phase10.config.js`, making 12 tracked paths in its own JSON. The local Git diff includes earlier phases too, so it cannot establish authorship by itself. Five family implementations account for the detailed Gemini edits; the other families were primarily preserved. The report's routes `/invitations/:slug` and `/admin/templates/:id` are not substituted for actual route factory patterns.

The original browser suite has four cases × six projects (24), with two catalog scenes and selected Boilerplate scenes. It is not ten-family coverage. The original axe call disabled contrast and checked only critical violations. Codex enables contrast and waits for the actual family root; early scans of a skeleton are not accepted as invitation scans. Fresh loaded scans found actual contrast/select issues and drove source repairs.

“Universal <50ms”, “all ten libraries MIT/Apache”, “100% media rights”, universal focus traps and all-family 320px perfection lack the claimed denominator/proof. Current upstream licenses include additional restrictions. Emitted family gzip sizes are well below 15kB for several families, contradicting the blanket 15–70kB statement. F10-36 belongs to Phase21; other rights/device/cultural/field gaps remain open.''')

