doc(names[17],titles[17],'''Skill use is phase-bounded, with one primary and at most two supporting roles at a time. The requested ui-ux-pro-max/frontend-design inform art-preserving diagnosis; code-reviewer and ui-styling inform source repair; StyleSeed routes to ss-audit; QA uses the repository specialist with Playwright. [Actual skill/query ledger](evidence/ux-laws-and-skill-use.json).

UX Pro Max commands actually ran and their outputs are saved. Motion guidance and web target-size distinctions fit. The modal query returned generic focus guidance, so it did not substitute for containment source/tests. The Khmer typography retry returned zero matches; project Khmer typography references supplied the fallback. Latin “wedding/romance” font suggestions were rejected. Gemini’s claimed search result summaries remain unverified without raw logs.

StyleSeed’s existing legacy bundle selects operations-console × product-ui × productivity × list. It is not permission to turn ten artist-owned invitations into operational cards. ss-audit core heuristics were applied; no numerical StyleSeed score or grammar-specific conformance certificate is invented.

'''+table(['Law/heuristic','Actual application','Evidence'],laws))

doc(names[18],titles[18],'''Opening controls were audited as behavior, not by a Skip text node. DigitalYes keeps a stable bypass while unfolding and removes its purchase bar until the invitation is open; timers are cleaned and reduced preference can interrupt. Emerald uses a native badge, avoids nested double keyboard handling, inerts hidden content and focuses main. Canva respects closed preview and focuses its newly mounted main. Floral/Royal/Celestial expose initial bypass without removing their normal art actions.

The timing ledger distinguishes automation wall time from click-to-next-painted-frame browser observations. It does not establish a universal p95 <50ms guarantee. Normal-motion illustrations, skipped state, reduced motion and applicable covers have separate records. WithJoy/Bliss are coverless; Boilerplate’s public default is already open while preview can start closed.

'''+'''[State coverage](evidence/family-state-coverage.json), [measured timing](evidence/opening-skip-timing.json), [geometry](evidence/viewport-geometry.json). Remaining states such as every family’s hidden-tab, failed CSS event, changed event, back-navigation and runtime preference transition are marked NOT_RUN where not explicitly exercised. Physical 200/400% zoom and OS forced colors require the manual protocol. A CSS screenshot is not hardware certification.''')

doc(names[19],titles[19],'''Boilerplate, WithJoy, DigitalYes and shared GalleryGrid now use the existing stacked Modal behavior for initial focus, keyboard containment, inert background, Escape and opener return. Original paper/photo composition remains family-owned. Native gallery buttons and visible arrows provide a pointer-free path; image position is announced. Bliss uses the same isolation while keeping its real child mounted so closing/reopening or switching language retains draft input.

Other families use existing native/shared dialogs. Their original tests and new family paints are retained; not every alternate gallery/map presentation and nested-removed-trigger sequence has fresh end-to-end proof. Empty/broken image and image-list changes are explicitly bounded in the state ledger.

Existing audio controllers retain gesture/promise/error semantics. The degradation fixture rejects play promises, blocks selected font/video resources and supplies missing imagery; it is not proof that physical iOS autoplay succeeds. The shared music hook’s existing tests cover stale play results, source changes, pause/error and unmount. Default-track rights remain open.

Venue diagrams are uploaded illustrations, not live Google maps. Existing saved directions/embed URL contracts remain; no coordinates, Maps key, booking capability or provider access was invented. External links keep source rel constraints. [Media inventory](evidence/media-license-asset-inventory.json), [keyboard/axe](evidence/a11y-keyboard-axe.json), [family states](evidence/family-state-coverage.json).''')

doc(names[20],titles[20],'''C10-001 is a real guest privacy repair: a token change remounts the guest form’s state boundary; denied lookup cannot resurrect cached private details; a submission completing after that authority unmounts cannot change the new URL, cache or receipt. Eight new tests prove three negative privacy cases and 401/403/409/429/500 failure/retry behavior. Existing language, saved-response and canonical submission tests remain.

Demo renderer forms are not API submissions. Their feedback explicitly says nothing is sent; injected PublicRsvpForm still owns slug/token/access identity and only confirms after its service acknowledgement. No backend endpoint, price, payment status, entitlement or hash algorithm changed.

The preview helper checks exact origin, source window, nonce and allowed message shape. Existing negative unit tests cover wrong origin/source/session, prototype-like keys, malformed arrays/fields, unknown types and top-level published-route inactivity. New browser injections target a real embedded `/templates/.../demo` channel; the wrong `/preview` Boilerplate fixture was corrected because that local-only lookup route has no Boilerplate data entry. [Preview outcomes](evidence/preview-negative-tests.json).

Same-origin allow-scripts + allow-same-origin is not isolation against arbitrary executable child code. These frames run the trusted application renderer; the nonce/source/origin protocol is the live editing authority, not a legal sandbox guarantee. No sandbox weakening or raw executable template system was added. Untrusted text is rendered as JSX; URL/media and serialization contracts retain their existing validators. Unknown JSON roundtrip and entitlement tests remain in full suites; no universal security certificate is claimed.

Protected backend/Flyway/payment/worker/manifests stay unchanged by Codex. C08-013 remains with identity/security, including old-hash compatibility/API tests and Khmer UTF8 bounds. No arbitrary frontend 72-character limit was added.''')

doc(names[21],titles[21],'''[Coverage data](evidence/family-state-coverage.json) identifies each actual family/project/viewport/motion/state visit; [geometry](evidence/viewport-geometry.json) and [axe/keyboard](evidence/a11y-keyboard-axe.json) retain observed values and failures. Ten families have 320/1440 engine samples; Chromium adds 360/390/768/1024/1920 plus 844×390, 820×430 and 768×390. No “4 cases per project proves ten families” extrapolation is used.

Khmer long names, combining marks, font failure and selected forced-colors degradation are separate samples. Actual rendered language attributes are retained alongside requested app locale; they are not assumed identical. Invitation-owned light/dark palettes are preserved and never forced into app-shell theme tokens.

Native reviewer queue: invitation/guest honorifics, parent titles, day/period ceremony wording, blessing/RSVP/demo notices, date/numeral pronunciations, and long names in the family cover/main screenshots. Keep exact current strings until native approval; a passing fixture is not linguistic acceptance.

The external protocols below cover hardware/AT/natural zoom and additional domain dependencies. Every historical external ID retains its original reproduction and an execution template in the cross-phase ledger. Do not convert “unavailable here” to verified.

'''+'''Equipment: real current iPhone/Safari/VoiceOver and low-end Android/Chrome/TalkBack, Windows high contrast and browser text/zoom controls; fictional owner/personalized invitations and EN/KM authored content. On each: open normally/with reduced motion, use Skip, traverse every section and dialog by touch and keyboard/AT, zoom 200/400%, rotate short landscape, raise virtual keyboard in RSVP, reject media/network, submit a disposable response and retry errors. Expect readable marks, no obscured focus/actions, no background dialog focus or other-guest details, preserved draft and truthful acknowledgement. Save build fingerprint, device/OS/browser/AT/zoom, numbered actions, expected/observed, redacted capture and named QA/native signoff. Owner: device/accessibility QA and Khmer reviewer; Phase16/18 functional breadth and Phase26 certification. NOT EXECUTED physically.''')

