doc(names[22],titles[22],'''The current build was emitted locally and every dist file is hashed/measured. Raw and gzip bytes use consistent units; source/build fingerprints accompany the final captures. [Payload and lab data](evidence/performance-and-payload.json).

'''+table(['Chunk','Raw bytes','gzip bytes'],[[Path(row['path']).name,row['bytes'],row['gzip_bytes']]for row in chunks])+'\n'+table(['Family','Cache','Repeats','Median route ready ms','Median LCP observation ms','Median CLS observation'],[[row['family'],row['cache'],row['n'],row['route_readiness_median_ms'],row['lcp_observation_median_ms'],round(row['cls_observation_median'],6)]for row in performance.get('final_lab_summary',[])])+'''
Family chunks are not total route cost: the shared main bundle, TemplateExperience, motion runtime, styles, fonts and requested media also load. Several family gzip sizes are below 15kB, so the old blanket range was false. No dependency was installed; the new shared lightbox is reused rather than duplicated.

The local lab separates fresh browser-context navigation from warm same-context navigation, three repeats for Silk/DigitalYes/Floral, fixed 390×844 reduced motion and mocked API/external request blocking. Readiness wall time, browser frame observation, resource bytes, paint/LCP/CLS and long tasks are observations, not field CWV or INP. Earlier and later samples with differing readiness/source/concurrency are not a valid causal before/after improvement claim. There is no agreed all-family numerical performance budget, low-power GPU certification or field population. Performance QA must set the budget and collect field p75/INP before release.''')

doc(names[23],titles[23],'''Intent: independently verify and repair bespoke renderer behavior while retaining artist identity, guest authority and the valuable dirty worktree. Overall review verdict: **Request Changes for complete Phase10/release acceptance**, with local repairs retained and externally owned gates explicit.

'''+table(['ID','Severity','Observed defect','Repair / proof'],[[id,severity,summary,repair+'; '+verification]for id,severity,summary,area,before,repair,verification in defects])+'\n'+table(['ID','Reproduction and expected outcome'],[[id,' → '.join(steps)]for id,steps in reproductions.items()])+'''
Each failing-before command/log is preserved in the machine register; later logs do not overwrite earlier red output. Gallery/Canva and skip occlusion also have real browser traces. New assertions test user-visible truth and authority, not internal state names. One inherited test expecting a fake receipt was changed to require the truthful demo status; Escape is dispatched from the active control as an actual browser key does. Historical Phase02 assertions remain unchanged.

Positive patterns: explicit stable-key registry precedence, server-owned access/prices, existing Modal stack/background restoration, canonical RSVP child delegation, original font/art stacks and unknown JSON projection/roundtrip tests all provided useful contracts. No style-only refactor or new framework was needed. Questions for owners: exact commercial media grants, native ceremony wording, complete device lab and agreed performance budgets. No unapproved legal decision or content replacement is implied.''')

doc(names[24],titles[24],'''The table is generated from commands actually invoked. Raw output retains counts, ANSI-clean interpretation, assertion failures, browser process crashes and environmental diagnostics. Runs with source/spec changing during investigation are diagnostic and not substituted for the final frozen-build acceptance. Fresh full app suites include route, registry, preview and content contracts without rerunning each nested suite redundantly.

'''+table(['Run ID','Exact invoked command','Exit','Seconds','Counts / outcome','Raw log'],command_rows())+'''
The first suites exposed source defects, test-selector/readiness/capture issues, and resource contention when full unit/lint work overlapped browser capture. The default browser comparator is run separately. A ten-navigation aggregate case gets a per-navigation budget; individual five-second readiness assertions were not inflated. Firefox SWGL process crashes are environmental browser failures, retained as nonpassing runs. No rerun erases a red result.

The 107-pass/65-skip/2-fail intermediate run retained two Windows WebKit stability-wait failures during DigitalYes's 1.3-second opening. A separate real-frame probe recorded a constant 89×44px target at y80, hit-testable and unobscured until automatic unmount. Font/animation readiness alone did not solve the automation wait. The final test explicitly verifies target hit testing, sends a native pointer click, asserts the Skip click was actually delivered, and requires main focus. It uses neither force-click nor a dispatched synthetic event; automatic reveal cannot satisfy the click-delivery assertion. Diagnostic trace/logs remain red. Normal art screenshots now await finite browser animations and eager media/fonts; infinite decorative motion is retained.

`git diff --check` exits2 for two pre-existing extra EOF blank lines in marketplace `components/templates.css` and `pages/BrowseTemplates.css`; the initial baseline names the same paths/lines. They were not silently reformatted. Runtime sources were frozen before the final build/browser acceptance. The superseded delivery-acceptance browser process was explicitly stopped after the final lightbox index correction; its nonzero exit is an intentional termination, not a finished-suite result. See run-termination-notes.json and the raw log. Earlier timed-out/capture-helper diagnostics are likewise retained.

The baseline admin build used its source default `http://localhost:5173`; the regression runner serves customer preview at `http://127.0.0.1:4173`. Eight cross-phase Studio failures and two extra Phase02 iframe failures were traced to that mismatch. Only the admin test artifact was rebuilt with process variable `VITE_USER_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4173`; no source/.env file or preview trust check was changed. The matched-origin Phase06 rerun passes 44/44; matched-origin Phase02 returns the original 26 pass/6 fail distribution. See local-build-environment.json and both red and corrected command logs.

The first shared-ID browser fixture omitted the dynamic published catalog record for `koupreng-demo-wedding`: four passed/two failed before a public API fixture was supplied. This is not a change to renderer identity or entitlement. Both shared identities and the unknown stable-code failure path subsequently pass in the composition suite. The first composition with the default ten workers observed one five-second catalog-count timeout (13 pass/1 fail); its error snapshot already contains all three correct cards. Controlled composition with two workers passes 14/14; one unchanged default repeat also passes 14/14. That is one timeout in two default executions, not guaranteed concurrency reliability. No assertion deadline changed. The original Phase10 smoke passes 24/24 with the default ten workers, and focused normal DigitalYes passes 6/6 with the default six workers.

Admin Happy DOM logs iframe/script/network limitations even when assertions pass. Browser emulation is not physical certification. Phase02 keeps its historical 26 pass/6 fail result; the current distinct run is listed exactly when executed. No provider/bank transaction, backend schema change or live MySQL certification was performed.''')

