handoff='''## Phase11.1 Gemini handoff — prepare only

Next owner: Gemini frontend implementation. Phase11 is Event Creation / Onboarding / Draft-Safe Wedding Wizard, followed by Phase11 Codex independent QA. It is not a renderer reskin or payment implementation. Read AGENTS/ROUTER/master Phase11, this audit and the actual final dirty tree. Re-detect HEAD and source hashes; do not substitute stale remote files or overwrite prior phases.

Inspect actual creation/onboarding routes (`/app/events/new`, legacy `/event/create`, `/create/wedding` and current router aliases) and their feature modules, event APIs, draft adapters/stores and template intent before editing. Map new/resumed event states, authenticated/denied/expired session, template continuation, event type, host/couple/family names, date/time/timezone, venue, programme days, uploads, draft save/resume/refresh, validation, back/next/direct wayfinding, conflicts, failed provider and publish/preview guards only where current source supports them.

Current source anchor: `features/events/onboarding/EventCreatePage.jsx`, `EventFields.jsx`, `eventFields.js`, `eventCreation.js`, `EventPhotoUpload.jsx`, invitation/media/catalog APIs and templateIntent/templateIdentity helpers. Host route `/app/events/new` owns creation. Builder aliases `/event/create`, `/create/wedding`, `/dashboard/events/create` and host `/dashboard/invitations/new` redirect there; `/create/wedding/:id` remains the guarded legacy builder. Current setup uses per-user `sessionStorage` key `koupreng.onboarding.${user.id}`, retains `clientRequestId`, saves a PRIVATE event and clears the session only after an acknowledged save before navigating to workspace/guided invitation. Read current RequiredPhotoEventCreation, EventCreatePage, MobileWizardRefinement and LanSafariCompatibility tests before changing these contracts. This is a source handoff, not Phase11 end-to-end approval.

Preserve stable slug/code/preset identity, all 38 aliases and ten family identities; keep server prices/entitlements/publish authority, USD/KHR, idempotent request identity, partial/nil and unknown serialized JSON, existing user media/fonts, preview source/origin/nonce/session and guest isolation. Real form success requires backend acknowledgement. Keep public/personalized secrets out of logs/artifacts and never use a demo receipt as real persistence. Preserve the optional keepMounted modal behavior and hosted RSVP input lifetime where reused.

Use mobile-first progressive disclosure with clear labels, EN/KM, real Khmer long text and keyboard enlargement, management light/dark only where applicable, accessible loading/empty/error/unauth/denied/expired/draft/conflict states, reduced motion and WCAG2.2 AA. Evaluate all ten UI references with exact component/source/license/builder-output scope; use project controls first. Run targeted UX Pro Max queries and record actual matches/rejected results. Use Nielsen/Jakob/Hick/Fitts/Gestalt/Doherty principles as observable behavior, not a token checkbox. Do not import the existing operations-console StyleSeed grammar into wedding art without an appropriate scoped contract.

Carry forward the full 57-ID ledger, five AUTH gates, nine Phase07 partial gates, C08-013, C09-001/002/003, D10-01–06, this F10 matrix and C10 register with original statuses, proof, exact owners and due gates. Media rights belong to content/legal and asset workflow; physical/native/field verification to QA/native reviewers; live ABA/Telegram to Phase21. Do not close them because local creation tests pass. BCrypt policy requires backend identity/security decision and compatibility/API tests, not frontend truncation.

Required Gemini output: actual source/diff attribution, route/state and template-continuation matrix, negative/positive request and draft tests, both app checks as relevant, source-bound before/after renders, performance/payload comparison under matched conditions, component/legal decisions, UX-law traceability and named unresolved owners. Demonstrate fresh and resumed save/refresh, errors, duplicate-submit prevention and template identity. Hand the package to Phase11 Codex independent QA; do not claim that QA already happened.

No Phase11.1 implementation, new capability, staging, commit, push, PR or deployment is authorized by this handoff artifact.
'''
doc(names[26],titles[26],'''The final source changes are exact paths, hashes and Codex-only patches in [the attribution ledger](evidence/changed-files-and-rollback.json). Previously dirty files must be restored only from the audited pre-Codex snapshot after checking no concurrent later edit; previous HEAD would lose earlier designers’ work. New Codex sources/tests can be selectively removed only after checking references. No rollback command was executed.

'''+table(['Modified existing path','Before hash','After hash','Selective diff'],[[row['path'],row['before_sha256'][:12],row['after_sha256'][:12],row['codex_only_diff']]for row in changedrows])+'''
All new paths and exact final tracked/untracked counts are machine-listed. Backend/Flyway/payment/worker sources and package manifests remain protected. Any later reviewer must compare hashes before reversal; untracked source is backed by local snapshots, not Git. Legal/media permissions, native copy, physical AT/devices/zoom, field metrics, broader state coverage and historical red assertions keep complete release acceptance open.

'''+handoff)
